WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.580
"I'll bring her a big Toblerone."

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.100
"I brought you a big Toblerone."

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.100
"You don't deserve this big Toblerone."

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.660
[Gigguk]: You know... out of context, this one clip may seem like it makes no sense

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.329
but trust me: When you see this IN context

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.090
it

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.920
makes even less fucking sense.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.779
So in some crazy alternate universe, this one guy from some band

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:27.080
decided he can make his own show about an anime world seen through the eyes of Jaden Smith.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.920
Starring Jaden Smith with big names like Jude Law, Susan Sarandon,

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.520
Stephen Fry, and Steve Buscemi providing some supporting roles.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:37.080
Oh.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.560
Wait... that was... that was... that was this universe.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.700
This is what happens when a group of millennial students more lit than Snoop Dogg on 420

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:50.100
break into the Netflix offices and describe a random episode of anime to some Netflix executive

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.900
and the executive decides to make an anime based on that description alone

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.200
...and the executive is Jaden Smith.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.300
[Jaden Smith]: Unbelievable.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:03.600
Now this is the part of the video where I'm supposed to tell you about Neo Yokio, but um...

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:04.840
um...

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.080
[Kaz]: I don't get it. How did you know the Helenas were gonna kill me?

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.200
[Helena]: I had a dream that a Toblerone was in trouble and that Toblerone was you.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.340
[Gigguk]: Neo Yokio is a Netflix exclusive

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:18.400
ani–

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.100
anim–

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.020
Uhh, excuse me...

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:29.300
A[Burp]nime that showcases the life of Kaz. a walking, talking personification of Jaden Smith's Twitter account.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.000
Starring Jaden Smith.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.440
Featuring Jaden Smith's voice acting.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:37.640
"I'm not obsessed with clothes. I'm just an elegant man of taste."

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:42.300
It chronicles Kaz's adventure in the 100% real anime city of San Fransokyo.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:43.820
Los Angelokyo.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.140
Neo Yokio.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.000
North Kakalaka.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.520
In the future independent weeaboo state of Japerica.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:53.500
I just made that up right now, but I wouldn't be surprised if that was actually true.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.920
He exorcises demons,

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.800
fights to become the number one bachelor,

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.520
becomes a communist driver,

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.640
and flies around on his mecha butler.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.800
Uh, what else?

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.900
"A demon possessed my field hockey ball!"

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.700
"Oh for fuck's sake."

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.180
[Gigguk]: Wait? Is this really an anime?

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.280
Nah, it's gotta be an anime. Look!

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:08.960
There's Ranma.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.500
There's Sailor Moon, who even knows anymore?

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.000
I mean, what was that thing I said literally three videos ago?

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.340
"If anime were to properly become mainstream  in the future, I believe Netflix will have a major part to play."

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.020
*(crying)*

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.700
(in horror) WE DID THIS!

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.000
THIS IS WHAT WE WANTED!

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.140
OH GOD, WHAT HAVE WE DONE?!?!

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:32.040
I mean, hey, who's this guy? Looks Japanese. Maybe he's worked in anime before.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.219
Probably nothing I've ever heard of. Must be a nobody. Studio Deen? Production IG?

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.420
Never heard of them. Do they make anime or something?

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.540
Must be some small studio that has done nothing.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.540
*crying/laughing who knows*

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:44.609
But to be fair, I think it was mostly animated by some Korean studio.

00:02:44.609 --> 00:02:46.980
I- I don't know, there's not much information about the production details of this.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.700
So you can just go ahead and take it down, r/Anime. Just- just take it down.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:51.880
We didn't– we didn't want this. Just give us Shelter, but

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.358
Take this down, take you, take, take this, TAKE THIS DOWN!!!!!!!!!!!!

00:02:54.389 --> 00:02:59.668
I had a full-on existential crisis trying to figure out exactly just how this thing exists.

00:02:59.669 --> 00:03:01.800
I mean WHAT IS THIS SHOW?!?!?

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.520
What IS it?! You have a production with the voice talents of Jude Law, Susan Sarandon,

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.760
Steve Buscemi and Stephen Fry in something that may or may not be an anime

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.400
And this is the way they mark their introduction to the medium.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.600
"WHAT IN THE NAME OF Shakespeare's arse is GOING ON HERE?"

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:20.400
That's a very... very good question.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.180
First of all, let's look at these character designs.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:25.300
They look like they were ripped from some kid's middle school DeviantART project

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.980
And the animation is not much better, looking like it came out of a mid-2000's anime.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.660
...And I'm not sure if that's an insult to mid-2000's anime.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:37.600
Eureka 7 came out in mid 2000s, Full Metal Alchemist came out in mid 2000's.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:41.280
Hell, I think even LoveHina had smoother animation than-

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:47.320
But, you know, it's not just about the aesthetics, which can be saved by equally good writing and plot.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:50.100
"What, do you live here?"

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.620
"I wish I lived here."

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.420
"Me too." *gigguk chuckling*

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.380
The writing boils down to this:

00:03:56.380 --> 00:04:01.700
Can you appreciate the enlightened knowledge that can be found on Jaden Smith's Twitter in such tweets as "how can mirrors be real?

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.900
"How can mirrors be real... if our eyes aren't real?"

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:10.940
"You can discover everything you need to know by looking at your hands." And...

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.180
"Most trees... are blue"

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:17.920
Well good, cuz this show plays out like scrolling through his Twitter feed. Nothing makes sense.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.760
Jude Law, why are you a mecha butler?

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.300
Why do people care about who is number one bachelor?

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:26.460
Did someone actually write an action in the scripts that reads:

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:28.240
"Vapes menacingly"

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:33.720
And hey, while we're at it, why not tackle some hot topics like gender politics, capitalistic ideals and communism?

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.620
"She seems like a bit of a nut."

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.720
"Have some sympathy, sir. She's from the Soviet Union."

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:44.920
"It is a social phenomenon in Japan that has isolated up to a million young people. It's known as hikikomori."

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:46.300
"I'm hikikomori now"

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.530
Nah, I gotta say though...

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:53.240
It's really good to see Western creators also tackling real social issues that are prevalent abroad...

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.000
"Hikikomori?"

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.100
"Hikikomori."

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.500
"Full hikikomori??"

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.100
"Hikikomori to the max."

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.280
(muffled) "Hikikomori."

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.980
"Hikikomori."
"Hikikomori?!"

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:07.790
And... I mean... the first step is always is just... using that word enough times so one day they'll hopefully figure out what it means.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:14.620
This is not even mentioning the most gaudy in-your-face product placements that are just insulting for anyone watching it.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:22.880
So it's really lucky that I have the cool refreshing taste of Heineken to get me through these troubling times.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:29.860
That wasn't a dig at their product placement. I just really like beer.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:34.060
...because this show turns me into a raging alcoholic.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:38.640
I keep thinking that any moment I'll wake up and realize that this was just some weird dream birth.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:41.060
Nope. I mean there's...no, it's uh... it's

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:45.800
It's 6 episodes... yeah, it's, it's still on Netflix. It's not a dream!!!

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:50.051
If you're going to watch it, I recommend watching it while intoxicated, but don't worry if you can't.

00:05:50.051 --> 00:05:53.409
Because after you watch it, you'll walk out feeling intoxicated either way.

00:05:53.409 --> 00:05:56.500
This is the worst piece of garbage to ever come out

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:00.460
And you should save yourself a few hours of your life by avoiding it like the plague.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:06.760
...Is what I would be saying, until about three episodes in I had an epiphany.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:11.500
Within this convoluted mess of a production, I was... having a good time.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:14.840
I was laughing. It was entertaining.

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:20.920
It had the same rhythm, jump cuts, awkward delivery, and comedic timing you'd see in something akin of an abridged series.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:22.340
"How thoughtful."

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.460
'Honey, the snacks are ready.'

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:27.540
"Guys I gotta go. Snacks are ready."

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:30.740
And then it hit me. This is comedy genius.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:38.660
This is the final form of anime. It is an abridged series for an anime that only exists in Jaden Smith's mind!

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:44.380
Forget what I said about the Netflix executives. It's Ezra Koenig waking up one day and thinking to himself:

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:48.730
'You know what? I feel like making the most expensive meme that's ever been made.'

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.660
It's so absurdly over the top with perfect material

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:55.060
That it's just rife with the best and worst of meme culture today.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:58.940
All it's missing is someone dabbing with a fidget spinner and a fedora and it'll be complete.

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.680
Wait. Hold on a second.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:03.060
[music in background] [ringtone]

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:06.380
"Charles, who's calling?"
"It's Aunt Agatha, sir."

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.040
"Put her through. Audio only."

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:12.240
"I said audio only!!" *Gigguk dabbing with a fidget spinner and a fedora*

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:17.280
This isn't just bad animation. The animation complements the amateur comedic tone

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:21.120
In the opposite way that Nichijou uses its animation for its absurd comedy

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:23.680
It's not bad animation at all, it's...

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:27.340
Sakuga! Jaden Smith isn't just talking shit.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:33.520
He's a philosopher way beyond our time and his wise words here should be listened to. Yes.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:40.220
It isn't Neo Yokio, it's Neo Wokio. When we think of iconic character tropes in anime, what do we see?

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:45.249
Tsunderes, yanderes, kuuderes. But move out the way, boys, because now is the era of

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:50.140
Toblerone-deres.You don't deserve this dere. YOU DON'T DESERVE IT.

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:56.340
Yes. This is the hottest new waifu of the season. Forget REM, forget fucking Megumin.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:08:02.840
How can they even hope to stand up to the chewy, milky, triangular sweetness of a Toblerone bar?

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:05.880
No I don't want to see just plain old chocolate bars any more.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:11.380
[interspersed with clapping] Posters, figurines, fucking edible dakimakuras. Come on J-LIST. Let's get on that shit.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:17.480
Overall I give Neo Yokio nine dabs out of ten. Right up there with Ghost Stories, but just shy of

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:22.980
The absolute masterpieces like the Bible Black dub and the magnum opus of them all: Garzey's wings.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.780
"DAMN YOU YAMATO TAKERUNO MIKOTOAOAUUUUUUGH!!!!!﻿"

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:29.400
And I un-ironically hope that there will be a sequel.

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:31.240
with Shia LaBeouf in it

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.320
Uhhhhh

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.360
Well that just happened. Hey guys, hope you enjoyed the video.

00:08:39.409 --> 00:08:44.415
Thank you very much this month to Robert Harnborg, Kmustlive, Basel, Lee Watts, Patrick Madsen,

00:08:44.415 --> 00:08:48.278
And everyone else on Patreon for helping support me for this month and making this video possible.

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:51.010
Not many updates today, but I am back in Thailand now.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:55.599
And I'm thinking about doing a meet-up, for now penciled in the date of Saturday the 14th of October

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:59.890
Just outside the Bangkok animates in the MBK center, at around 2 p.m.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:02.589
So if you're in the Bangkok area, feel free to come say hi.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:06.358
I've also made a Facebook event in the description just in case any last-minute changes happen.

00:09:06.358 --> 00:09:12.190
Or so I can just get an idea of numbers because I really don't know how many of you guys are in Bangkok. Anyway. That's it from me.

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:14.980
I've been Gigguk and I'll see you all next time.

